The '''Estado Nuevo''' ({{lit|New State}}), was a pivotal period in [[History of Balisca|Baliscan history]], spanning from the onset of the [[Great Adonian War]] in the late 1930s through the onset of the [[Adonian Depression]] in the late-1940s. Characterized by a strategic, albeit temporary, re-consolidation of certain political powers under the [[Confederal government of Balisca|confederal government]], the Estado Nuevo represented Balisca's pragmatic adaptation to unprecedented global challenges.

Faced with the severe, though domestically mitigated, economic strain of the Depression and the escalating threat of [[W:Fascism|global fascism]] and [[W:Rearmament|re-armament]] leading into the Great Adonian War, the nation consciously shifted some authority back to its central organs to ensure coordinated national defense, economic stability, and effective international engagement. This period notably saw the establishment of bodies like the [[Instituto por la Reconstrución Industrial|IRI]] in 1933, which controlled significant portions of the national economy, demonstrating a willingness to centralize economic guidance to navigate the crises. The Estado Nuevo was thus a testament to Balisca's capacity for adaptive governance, balancing its core tenets of [[W:Decentralization|decentralization]] and [[W:Local autonomy|local autonomy]] with the urgent demands of national survival on the global stage.

